# 2023 quiz boundaries

- Read AGENTS.md, docs/loop-engineer.md and outputs/quiz-2023-scope-revision.json. The active plan is quiz-2023-v2.0.0, Q001-Q030; prior L/C tasks are historical evidence only.
- The owner confirmed 23 July 2023 Congress scope. Reconcile all 52 constituencies and every real candidacy, including minor and territorial lists; search/download every applicable programme and retain missing-source records.
- Agent source acquisition is authorized. Keep bounded original files/extractions in the ignored local cache; track reproducible provenance/hashes/applicability and authored analysis. Downloaded, extracted and fully read are different statuses.
- Read every available programme in full one by one, including annexes/footnotes; cross-reference the programmes and directly author questions, explanations, rubrics and numeric positions. No automatic question/position generator. Deterministic extraction/validation and selection among authored IDs are allowed.
- Target 80 distinct useful questions; release at least 60 across ten or more topics. Do not pad, repeat measures or fabricate missing positions. Exact context/conditions/negation/quantities/locators accompany every scored claim; unknown/conflict is unscored.
- Label intro/results/exports as the 2023 edition; never relabel old positions as current or inherit a coalition member programme without applicable evidence.
- Quiz first. Programme-comparison UI, feedback expansion and optional translations are deferred; retain compact source disclosures. No new backoffice, account, reviewer workforce, runtime model or infrastructure.
- Write for ordinary people: one concrete decision, everyday Spanish, short neutral help and understandable agreements/differences. No jargon prerequisite, analyst dashboard, leading moral answer or invented policy impact.
- Verify ordered -2..+2 labels, stored answers, proposition polarity, cited party value, weighted contribution and result explanation. Strong disagreement with a supporting position must be a per-question disagreement even if aggregate overlap is high.
- Answers/priorities/province/affinities stay in browser memory. Same fixed public bank for all. Order only a disclosed fixed evidence-qualified subset using identical questions/weights; keep all other eligible candidacies visible. No personalised API/URL/log or silent minor-party exclusion.
- Ten balanced starters then optional five-question blocks through thirty where useful evidence remains. Explicit finish before party reveal; skip/unsure are not neutral; overlap is not probability or a voting instruction.
- One-question design with credible neutral colours, clear selected/focus states, readable labelled choices and short reduced-motion-safe transitions. No timer, speed reward, correct/wrong opinion or party-coloured answers.
- Metrics stay disabled and deferred. Future optional collection still requires separate opt-in, bounded randomized contributions, truthful notice and actual host/log verification; no guarantee of anonymity/unique voters.
- Reuse Laravel/static bundles/SQLite and existing CI/citation/hash/recovery utilities. Pin sessions and support corrections/withdrawal/rollback; prepare a separately analysed future edition when new programmes arrive.
- Work directly on main, preserve files/index/signed history. Exact staged CI before every commit, no bypass/reset/rewrite/automatic push. Prior implementation chat remains paused; no scheduler is started. PUBLIC-LAUNCH is the concrete external-action boundary.
